/A 1355 0 R
/Alt (Schematic diagram outlining the process of coating a silk fiber with a 2-HEMA layer and embedding it in PVA hydrogel. Step A shows chemical structures of 2-HEMA and PVA with hydrophilic groups labeled. Step B illustrates plasma treatment of a silk fiber. Step C depicts UV light activating hydroxyl groups on the fiber, followed by reaction with 2-HEMA. Step D shows radical formation and attachment of 2-HEMA. Step E adds more 2-HEMA chains. Step F displays bonding between the 2-HEMA-coated fiber and PVA chains. Step G depicts a cross-section with a silk fiber at the center, surrounded by a 2-HEMA-coated layer and PVA hydrogel.)
/K [9 1356 0 R]
/P 104 0 R
/Pg 47 0 R
/S /Figure
